@petrochenkov: Here's an alternative approach:

Since we will only ever need to decode `Spans` from upstream crates, we actually have all of the necessary information available inside `register_crate` (after `resolve_crate_dep` is called). We then construct a `FxHashmap<CrateNum, Lrc<Once<Vec<ImportedSourceFile>>>` mapping each dependency to its `Once`, and pass it to the new `CrateMetadata`.

This avoids the need for any locking - we don't need to care about any crates registered that may be registered later on, since the newly registered crate will never need to decode anything from them. We still need a `Lrc` to avoid repeatedly cloning a `Vec<ImportedSourceFile>>`, but this seems unavoidable without making invasive changes to metadata decoding (e.g. requiring a `CStore` in the tuple that implements `Metadata`).

